import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base title="Old Forest Echoes"><header class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">Music · Art · Forest protection</p><h1>Old Forest <em>Echoes.</em></h1><p>Ikimetsän kaiku — fall in love with old growth forests through music and art composed and performed there.</p></header><section class="section split"><img class="portrait" src={`${base}images/nuku-nuku-cover.webp`} alt="Barbora Xu with her guzheng in the forest" loading="lazy" /><div class="prose"><p>Barbora is the founder of the Old Forest Echoes project and association, devoted to protecting old growth forests through artistic work.</p><p>In collaboration with the Finnish Nature League (Luonto-Liitto), and with support from the Kone Foundation, the project raises awareness and resources to protect threatened old growth forests in Finland.</p><p>Music grows out of time spent in the forests, from spring to autumn. Concerts and workshops invite audiences into the places that inspired the compositions, alongside land art, soundscapes, music videos and documentary filmmaking.</p><p>The project’s timeline runs from January 2025 to April 2027. Album sales and donations are intended to help purchase a patch of old growth forest and donate it to Luonnonperintösäätiö for protection.</p><a class="button" href={site.projectUrl}>Visit Old Forest Echoes ↗</a><p class="credit">Photography · Jussi Vierimaa</p></div></section></Base>
